Package: phenoscapR
Title: Read, Analyse, and Visualise Akoya Spatial Biology Data
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R:
    person("phenoscapR contributors", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "phenoscapr@example.com")
Description: Provides an S4 class ('AkoyaExperiment') and a pipe-friendly
    workflow for reading, processing, analysing, and visualising multiplexed
    spatial biology data produced by Akoya Biosciences platforms
    (PhenoCycler, CODEX, PhenoImager) and QuPath. Supports three input
    formats ('processor', 'inform', 'qupath') with automatic detection.
    Functions cover the full analysis pipeline from importing cell
    segmentation outputs through quality control, marker normalisation,
    cell phenotyping, spatial statistics (nearest neighbour distances,
    Ripley's K, Moran's I, neighbourhood enrichment, pair correlation),
    spatial clustering, Delaunay network construction, and publication-ready
    visualisations including spatial maps, violin plots, dot plots,
    composition bar plots, ridge plots, and spatial network graphs.
    A configurable colour palette system supports viridis palettes and
    custom gradients from user-defined anchor colours.
